  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "BIP-340 is the Bitcoin Improvement Proposal that standardises Schnorr signatures for use on the Bitcoin network, using the secp256k1 elliptic curve. It defines a 64-byte signature scheme that is provably secure in the random oracle model and enables key and signature aggregation through protocols such as MuSig2. BIP-340 is a prerequisite for Taproot (BIP-341) and introduces substantial efficiency and privacy improvements over the legacy ECDSA scheme. The specification includes a deterministic signing algorithm and rigorous test vectors to facilitate cross-implementation compatibility.",
